    46	      <aside class="three-things" data-layer="fact">
    47	        <p class="tt-label">Three things to know</p>
    48	        <ol>
    49	          <li>Judge Christopher Cooper denied Representative Joyce Beatty's request for an emergency hearing on September 17. In the same minute order, he required written notice more than 30 days before the defendants implement a change to the project plans previously presented to the court, including demolition of the main building.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="more than 30 days before the implementation of any changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court" /></li>
    50	          <li>The reproduced sentence does not say that every physical change is covered or state whether demolition would be lawful. It makes notice turn on changes to the scope of the project plans previously presented to the court.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court" /></li>
    51	          <li>The executive director said the immediate closure was a seven-day safety measure unless extended. The defendants characterized it as separate from the board's renovation decision.<Cite s="floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17" passage="which will last for seven days, unless extended" /><Cite s="defendants-response-86-2026-09-17" passage="separate from any Board decision related to closure for ongoing renovations" /></li>
    52	        </ol>
    53	      </aside>
    54	
    55	      <p class="railed rail-note" data-layer="fact">The federal docket's September 17 minute order was not available as a court-hosted document in the public sources we could preserve. UPI reproduces the operative sentence below in full. Beatty's counsel quotes part of it and describes the requirement as 30 days' advance warning; the surrounding motions, declarations, earlier opinions and board records are preserved separately.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events" /><Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="any changes to the scope of the project plans" /><Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="30 days’ advance warning" /></p>
    56	
    57	      <div data-layer="proof" class="event-record-context">
    58	        <p class="sources-line">This story rests on filings in Beatty v. Trump and D.C. Preservation League v. Trump; the court's May 29 opinions; the board's August meeting record; the August 28 joint report; the September 16 scheduling order; federal statutes governing the Kennedy Center; the September 17 minute order as reproduced in full by UPI and quoted in part by Beatty's counsel; and the coverage records checked against those documents.</p>
    59	      </div>
