    61	      <section id="what-happened">
    62	        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The request and the ruling</p>
    63	        <h2 data-layer="fact">The judge refused the hearing and added an advance-notice rule</h2>
    64	        <p data-layer="narrative">Beatty asked for an emergency hearing after the main building closed and after the board voted to close it for renovation. The defendants answered that the immediate closure was separate from the renovation decision. Executive Director Matt Floca described it as a temporary safety measure and declared that structural deterioration created acute risks to public safety. He said the initial closure would last seven days unless extended.<Cite s="beatty-motion-84-2026-09-16" passage="MOTION FOR EMERGENCY HEARING" /><Cite s="defendants-response-86-2026-09-17" passage="separate from any Board decision related to closure for ongoing renovations" /><Cite s="floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17" passage="acute risks to public safety resulting from continued structural deterioration" /><Cite s="floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17" passage="which will last for seven days, unless extended" /></p>
    65	        <p data-layer="narrative">The filing also put two public signals before Cooper. Trump had told reporters that without recognition for his administration's role in the renovation and fundraising, the building would close and end up being ripped down. The filing included a photograph of him reading a placard that appeared to say “Kennedy Center DEMOLISHED.” ABC reported that the published images did not show the entire placard and that the visible word was cut off at “DEMOLIS.” A Kennedy Center spokesperson separately said that nothing was being demolished.<Cite s="beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17" /><Cite s="beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17" passage="it will end up being ripped down" /><Cite s="beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17" passage="appears to read “Kennedy Center DEMOLISHED.”" /><Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="The published images don't show the entire placard" /><Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="cut off as “DEMOLIS.”" /><Cite s="cbs-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="nothing is being demolished" /></p>
    66	        <p data-layer="narrative">Cooper denied the hearing. He nevertheless ordered the defendants to give plaintiffs in both cases written notice before implementing a covered change.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="Beatty's request for a hearing was denied" /><Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="provide such notice in writing to Plaintiffs in both cases" /></p>
    67	        <QuoteCard speaker="U.S. District Judge Christopher Cooper" when="September 17, 2026" where="Minute order, as reproduced by UPI; bracketed explanations are UPI's">
    68	          <p>To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events, the Court hereby ORDERS Defendants [the Kennedy Center board] to provide such notice in writing to Plaintiffs in both cases more than 30 days before the implementation of any changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court in D.C. Preservation League [a separate case], including but not limited to any 'demolition' of the Center's main building.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events" /></p>
    69	        </QuoteCard>
    70	        <p data-layer="narrative">The order also required the administration to update Cooper by September 23 on the status of the temporary closure and emergency repairs.<Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="update him on the status of the" /><Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="emergency repairs" /> Beatty's counsel said Cooper “ordered discovery into the Board’s actions related to a potential demolition.”<Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="ordered discovery into the Board’s actions related to a potential demolition" /> UPI published only an excerpt of the order; the “ordered discovery” wording is counsel's account.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="But he added another order" /></p>
    71	      </section>
